<title>USA: Clinton releases emergency aid for Dakotas.</title>
<headline>Clinton releases emergency aid for Dakotas.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-01-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton Wednesday released $5 million in emergency Low Income Home Energy Assistance Program funds to help residents of North and South Dakota deal with an unusually harsh winter.</p>
<p>The action helps low income families pay for fuel and buy materials to insulate their homes. North Dakota will receive nearly $2.8 million and South Dakota an additional $2.2 million.</p>
<p>Last week, Clinton declared both states federal disaster areas because of the severity of winter storms that have struck the Dakotas.</p>
</text>
